# Cloudflare Pages: headers for the static files in this project.
#
# Only the front page's own files. /api/* responses come from Functions and set
# their own headers, and the games behind the router are separate projects with
# their own _headers.
#
# The CSP is the second line of defence for the session token in localStorage:
# without inline or foreign script, an injected <script> has nothing to run.
# Add an origin here before adding a script, stylesheet, font or analytics
# beacon that needs one, or it will be blocked.
#
# Outside origins, and why:
# - Google Fonts: the fonts (style-src, font-src).
# - Google AdSense and its consent message (src/account/ads.ts): the ad tag and
#   what it loads (script-src), ad and consent frames (frame-src), ad requests,
#   measurement and fraud checks (connect-src), Google's pixels (img-src). The
#   ads themselves render in frames on other origins, under their own policy,
#   and cannot read this page.
#
#   script-src names only the hosts the tag was seen loading script from. Keep
#   broad Google hosts out of it: www.google.com and the doubleclick and
#   gstatic hosts serve JSONP and other scripts an injected <script src> could
#   abuse, so allowing them would undo most of this policy. Add a host only
#   after seeing it blocked in the console, and only the exact host.
#
# What an AdSense script on this origin can reach: the page, and localStorage
# with the 30-day session token. That is accepted on purpose, with two limits:
# the admin API needs a separate PIN-issued token that only lives in memory
# (issueAdminToken in shared/account-server.js), and pages where a PIN is typed
# never load the tag (src/lib/adFreePages.ts). See "Ads (Google AdSense)" in
# docs/OPERATIONS.md before widening any of this.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://*.adtrafficquality.google; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://www.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://tpc.googlesyndication.com https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://adtrafficquality.google https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://*.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; frame-src https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://tpc.googlesyndication.com https://*.safeframe.googlesyndication.com https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://www.google.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Vite puts a content hash in every file name under /assets, so a changed file
# is a new URL and the old one can be cached for good.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
